HST Office packaging: macOS dmg for a product name with a space.

PRODUCTNAME "HST Office" made the dmg step of the installer fail on macOS:
 - the hdiutil command line passed the package folder and the archive path
   ("HST Office_<version>_MacOS_<arch>") unquoted;
 - the language pack step looked for "<PRODUCTNAME>.app", but the bundle in the
   installation set is "<PRODUCTNAME_WITHOUT_SPACES>.app" (HSTOffice.app), so its
   tar of Contents/ failed.
Both are behaviour-neutral for names without spaces (LibreOffice, LibreOfficeDev).
Only the macOS dmg path of simplepackage.pm is touched; deb/msi/archive are unchanged.

License: modified upstream file keeps its license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/solenv/bin/modules/installer/simplepackage.pm
+++ b/solenv/bin/modules/installer/simplepackage.pm
@@ -295,7 +295,9 @@
             # LanguagePack and HelpPack files are collected in $srcfolder, packaged into
             # tarball.tar.bz2 and finally the Language Pack.app is assembled in $appfolder
             $localtempdir = "$tempdir/$packagename";
-            my $srcfolder = $localtempdir . "/" . $volume_name_classic_app . "\.app";
+            # The bundle directory is named PRODUCTNAME_WITHOUT_SPACES.app (configure INSTROOTBASESUFFIX).
+            (my $bundle_name = $volume_name_classic_app) =~ s/ //g;
+            my $srcfolder = $localtempdir . "/" . $bundle_name . "\.app";
 
             $volume_name             .= " " . $$languagestringref . " Language Pack";
             $volume_name_classic     .= " Language Pack";
@@ -477,7 +479,7 @@
         # bzip2 should be smaller than with lzfse. A .dmg built from a debug
         # build was 262M with bzip2 and 273MB for lzfse. So it appears that
         # lzfse creates .dmg files that are only 4% or 5% larger than bzip2.
-        $systemcall = "cd $localtempdir && hdiutil create -megabytes $megabytes -srcfolder $folder $archive -ov -fs HFS+ -volname \"$volume_name\" -format ULFO";
+        $systemcall = "cd \"$localtempdir\" && hdiutil create -megabytes $megabytes -srcfolder \"$folder\" \"$archive\" -ov -fs HFS+ -volname \"$volume_name\" -format ULFO";
         if (( $ref ne "" ) && ( $$ref ne "" ) && system("hdiutil 2>&1 | grep unflatten") == 0) {
             $systemcall .= " && hdiutil unflatten $archive && Rez -a $$ref -o $archive && hdiutil flatten $archive &&";
         }
